%% alt: Model output passes four checks in order: shape (does it parse and match the schema), grounding (is it supported by the sources), policy, and safe handling, before it reaches the user or a downstream system. A failure at any of the first three leads to a retry, a fallback, a refusal or an escalation.
flowchart TB
  M[Model output]:::model --> S[Shape]:::control --> G[Grounding]:::control --> P[Policy]:::control --> H[Safe handling]:::control --> D[User or<br/>downstream system]:::human
  S & G & P -.->|fail| F[Retry, fall back,<br/>refuse or escalate]:::tool
